---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, REPO_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="About Nod"
  description="Who makes Nod, how to reach them, and what the app and this site do with your data. Short version: everything stays on your machine."
>
  <SiteNav cta={{ href: "/downloads", label: "Download" }} />

  <main>
    <section class="wrap about">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="about__title">Made by one person who reviews a lot of PRs.</h1>

      <div class="about__body">
        <p>
          Nod is built by me, Paulius Krutkis, a software engineer. I got tired
          of reviewing pull requests in a browser tab, so I built the tool I
          wanted: something that treats the review queue like an inbox and
          keeps my hands on the keyboard.
        </p>
        <p>
          The source is available on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>. Bug
          reports and feature requests are welcome in the{" "}
          <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>, or write to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="about__head" id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
      <div class="about__body">
        <p>
          The app has no telemetry, no analytics, and no account with me. Your
          GitHub or GitLab token is stored on your machine and sent only to
          the Git host it belongs to. Left alone, the app talks to two kinds
          of servers: your Git host, to fetch and submit reviews, and GitHub
          releases, to check for updates.
        </p>
        <p>
          The one thing that can add a third is ask-about-code, which is
          optional and does nothing until you paste in an API key of your
          own. When you do, the code you ask about goes to the provider that
          key belongs to, and to nobody else. I never see it, and there is no
          account or subscription in between.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site sets no cookies. Traffic is measured with Cloudflare Web
          Analytics, which is cookieless and aggregate: no identifiers on
          your device, no cross-site tracking. The hosting network keeps
          standard server logs.
        </p>
        <p>
          If any of this changes, for example when purchasing opens and a
          payment provider gets involved, this page changes with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding-top: clamp(56px, 10vh, 104px);
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  .about__title {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.4vw, 2.9rem);
    font-weight: 640;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .about__head {
    margin-top: 56px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 620;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .about__body {
    margin-top: 16px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .about__body a {
    color: var(--fg);
  }
</style>
